# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 131's class, lane recovery-b2 (lane recovery-b1's
# report, U5). Symptom: a signature whose `(` never closed named its missing
# `)` beside the lexer's `unclosed_bracket`, at the body's first word, and the
# body, which the lexer read inside the bracket and laid out as no block, was
# then refused line by line at the top level: `function f(a: i64` over
# `print(a)` cost `expected_params_close` at `print`, and with a declaration
# below, `expected_declaration` too. Cause: the parameter list sought its
# closer as a call's did before
# `fixedbugs-131-a-group-a-call-or-an-index-the-lexer-found-open`, and the
# body's absence was said as any other. Now the list ends at its line end no
# `,` goes on from and names no closer; a head whose line holds an opener
# the lexer named, with lines below in that opener's reach, leaves its body
# unsaid, a declaration's head passing those lines over to where the lexer
# named it and a statement's reading them as its block's own
# (`parse/unclosed.swallows_the_body`). A head with nothing in the reach
# still has its body named missing, at the next declaration, a mistake of
# its own.

function one_parameter(a: i64  #~ unclosed_bracket
    print(a)

function two_lines_of_them(a: i64,  #~ unclosed_bracket
        b: i64
    print(a + b)

function a_result_on_its_line(a: i64 -> i64  #~ unclosed_bracket
    return a

function generic<T>(v: T  #~ unclosed_bracket
    print(1)

constant K: [i64  #~ unclosed_bracket
    [1]

function nothing_below(a: i64  #~ unclosed_bracket

# The missing body is named at the next declaration's first word.
function an_if(n: i64)  #~ missing_body
    if f(n  #~ unclosed_bracket
        print(n)
    print(2)

function a_while(n: i64)
    while (n > 0  #~ unclosed_bracket
        print(n)

function a_for()
    for x in [1, 2  #~ unclosed_bracket
        print(x)

function a_match(n: i64)
    k = match f(n  #~ unclosed_bracket
        0 => 1
        _ => 2
    print(k)

function main()
    print(1) )  #~ expected_end_of_line
